# kills: an unknown BUILT-IN deck id falls back silently; a missing custom: id says so
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^an.unknown.BUILT.IN.deck.id.falls.back.silently..a.missing.custom..id.says.so$ tests/app.test.js
# The missing-custom-deck fallback goes silent, so a user whose saved scale is
# gone just sees a different deck with no explanation.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -4866,8 +4866,6 @@
 // renamed deck and falls back SILENTLY, as it always has. A missing custom: id
 // means the user's own saved scale is gone - deleted, or dropped as corrupt -
 // and a silent switch would look like the app lost their deck, so say so.
-if (wantedDeck !== deckId && wantedDeck.indexOf("custom:") === 0)
-  say("That deck is gone. Showing " + deck().name + ".", "warn");
 // A page route in the address bar at boot is a RELOAD of a page, or a link
 // someone pasted. Neither reopens it: #edit-<id> names a deck this session may
 // not have, and a page restored with no entry behind it is one the back
